From 6aa3819c84998d1c84f750789ebfb34afdd7f5cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashish Kumar Singh <ashishkmr472@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:18:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [XLA:GPU] A compile over a device memory limit stops after
 buffer assignment

xla_gpu_memory_limit_early_exit_bytes: where a module's buffer assignment holds more device bytes than it
(argument + output - alias + temp, as CompiledMemoryStats states them), its compile emits no code and its
executable states its memory and buffer assignment as a whole compile's do and fails to execute; within it,
the compile finishes. One compile decides whether a program fits a device's memory, rather than a compile
stopped after buffer assignment followed by a whole one.
